# fixture: retirement-sells-a-rental  (adversarial)
#
# a life event that closes a capital asset: Retire, in January 2028, ends
# the paycheck and sells a rental with a $300k gain. Life events fire on the
# month's first tick, before the assets' clocks move, so the sale recorded
# its capital-gains tax and proceeds a month early, in December 2027, while
# the figures booked them in January. No quick-start profile closes anything
# but a paycheck, which records nothing.

